  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nCyclonic flow around a large area of low pressure centered over the \nCanadian Maritimes will provide northerly flow and considerable \nclouds downwind of the Great Lakes today into tonight. A weak\ndisturbance could bring a period or two of very light drizzle early \nthis morning, but otherwise conditions will remain dry.\n\nSurface high pressure will build into the Ohio Valley tonight with\ndecreasing clouds and light winds. We can't rule out areas of fog\ndeveloping early Monday morning if skies clear early enough.\n\nMid-level ridging will nudge east into our area during the day on \nMonday. This will cause a slow warmup with afternoon highs reaching \ninto the 50s Monday and Tuesday, then near 60 degrees by Wednesday. \nThis dry and mild weather pattern will continue through the rest of \nthe week.",
